E resolved link type'","outbound_links.py:154-177 walks canonical (relation, other_key, opaque_vendor_type) and today emits type=opaque_vendor_type (the ACTUAL remote type)","link_direction.py:20 JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION = {'Blocks':'blocks','Relates':'relates_to'} is a FIXED reverse map; resolve_inbound_link (backend.py:301) returns relation=None for any vendor type outside it","Consequence 1: after remap relates_to->'Relationship', a remote 'Relationship' link resolves relation=None -> _diff_link_removals skips at outbound_links.py:157, so a deliberate local unlink of a remapped link is never propagated (the churn the REMOVE pass exists to stop)","Consequence 2: a pre-remap remote 'Relates' link resolves to relates_to -> _resolve_link would emit type='Relationship' for a link whose real remote type is 'Relates', so the applier resolving link id by (type,to_key) targets a nonexistent link"],"finding":"The REMOVE path cannot honour AC3 ('remapped relation's REMOVE targets the overridden link type') as specified, because the canonical remote-link set derives `relation` from the ACTUAL remote vendor type through a config-unaware built-in reverse map (link_direction.JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION / resolve_inbound_link), so emitting the OVERRIDE vendor_type on remove is incorrect and can also silently drop remaps.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6077fc237a4a4bcd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3, REMOVE bullet ('emit type=vendor_type (the OVERRIDE when remapped)') and AC line 3","norm_id":"n6951e84e12a9a4d5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project remaps relates_to to a custom link type, then a user removes a local relates_to dep whose remote link already exists","A relates_to link created before the remap config was added is later unlinked locally"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"On the REMOVE path emit type=opaque_vendor_type (preserve today's behaviour, since that string 